WEBVTT

00:00.620 --> 00:01.920
Satoru.

00:01.920 --> 00:03.490
Show him to the dorm.

00:03.770 --> 00:06.940
Explain the security and 
everything else to him, too.

00:07.280 --> 00:07.910
Huh?

00:09.680 --> 00:10.980
You pass.

00:10.980 --> 00:12.960
Welcome to Jujutsu Tech.

00:14.580 --> 00:15.820
Fushiguro!

00:15.820 --> 00:17.720
You look like you're doing well now.

00:17.720 --> 00:20.200
There were plenty of other 
empty rooms, weren't there?

00:20.200 --> 00:22.700
But isn't livelier better?

00:22.700 --> 00:24.320
I thought it'd be good for—

00:23.390 --> 00:25.480
Classes and missions are enough.

00:25.480 --> 00:26.840
This was an unwelcome favor.

00:26.840 --> 00:29.400
Wow, it's so organized.

00:29.400 --> 00:32.740
I just said you're unwelcome!

00:33.140 --> 00:35.270
Well, it's all good.

00:35.270 --> 00:37.510
More importantly, we're heading out tomorrow!

00:37.700 --> 00:41.050
We're gonna go pick up the third first-year.

00:44.580 --> 00:50.660
The train bound for Shibuya and 
Shinagawa is now arriving on track 1.

00:51.450 --> 00:55.360
For your safety, please 
stand behind the yellow line.

00:56.020 --> 00:57.360
Saori-chan.

00:59.480 --> 01:01.360
I'm here.

01:06.520 --> 01:07.780
I'm in Tokyo!

01:10.070 --> 01:12.900
How are there only three first-years? 
Isn't that too few?

01:12.900 --> 01:17.200
Well, have you ever met anyone 
who can see curses before?

01:19.160 --> 01:20.010
Nope.

01:20.010 --> 01:23.520
That just proves how small 
a minority jujutsu sorcerers are.

01:23.520 --> 01:26.270
Also, didn't you say I was the third?

01:26.530 --> 01:29.520
Their entry was decided a while ago.

01:29.520 --> 01:35.300
Tokyo Metropolitan
Jujutsu Technical High School

01:30.310 --> 01:32.040
You know what our school's like.

01:32.550 --> 01:34.260
Everyone has unique circumstances.

01:35.950 --> 01:37.650
Sorry for the wait.

01:37.650 --> 01:38.270
Oh?

01:39.090 --> 01:40.710
Your uniform made it in time, I see.

01:40.710 --> 01:42.640
Yeah, it's a perfect fit.

01:42.640 --> 01:45.110
Though it's slightly 
different from Fushiguro's.

01:45.430 --> 01:46.700
It has a hood, for one.

01:46.700 --> 01:50.340
That's because the uniforms can 
be customized upon request.

01:50.340 --> 01:51.020
Huh?

01:51.460 --> 01:53.740
But I never put in any requests.

01:53.740 --> 01:56.800
I was the one who put in the custom order.

01:58.720 --> 02:00.170
Whatever, I guess.

02:00.170 --> 02:03.640
Be careful. Gojou-sensei has a 
tendency to do things like that.

02:04.390 --> 02:07.060
More importantly, why are 
we meeting up in Harajuku?

02:07.060 --> 02:09.090
Because it's what she asked for.

02:09.090 --> 02:11.160
Hey, popcorn! I want some!

02:11.760 --> 02:14.740
Oh, hello there. Are you 
on the clock right now?

02:14.740 --> 02:16.530
No, I'm not.

02:16.530 --> 02:19.140
You see, I'm looking for potential models.

02:19.370 --> 02:21.070
This is who I am.

02:21.070 --> 02:22.860
Would you be interested?

02:22.860 --> 02:24.250
I'm in a hurry right now.

02:24.250 --> 02:26.560
Just hear me out!

02:28.400 --> 02:29.630
Hey, you.

02:30.070 --> 02:31.130
What about me?

02:32.410 --> 02:33.650
Her?!

02:34.860 --> 02:36.570
For the modeling gig, duh.

02:36.570 --> 02:38.560
I'm asking what you think about me.

02:38.560 --> 02:41.430
Oh, um, I'm in a hurry at the moment...

02:43.720 --> 02:44.640
What the hell?

02:44.640 --> 02:46.780
Don't run from me! Come out and say it!

02:46.780 --> 02:49.580
We're about to go talk to her?

02:48.660 --> 02:50.770
I'm sorry! Please let me go!

02:50.770 --> 02:52.840
This is kinda embarrassing.

02:53.490 --> 02:54.610
So are you.

02:54.610 --> 02:55.750
Hey!

02:55.750 --> 02:57.010
Over here!

02:57.010 --> 02:59.980
Damn, what's up with that blindfold?

03:00.860 --> 03:05.290
400 Yen Corner

03:03.510 --> 03:05.290
Okay, once again.

03:06.120 --> 03:07.790
Kugisaki Nobara.

03:07.790 --> 03:10.770
Be happy, boys. 
I'm the one woman in your group.

04:42.240 --> 04:49.160
Stare...

04:45.510 --> 04:51.730
Episode 3: Girl of Steel

04:47.040 --> 04:49.960
I'm Itadori Yuuji. I'm from Sendai.

04:50.240 --> 04:51.740
Fushiguro Megumi.

04:52.650 --> 05:03.160
Kugisaki's POV

04:53.320 --> 04:55.330
He looks like a potato.

04:55.330 --> 04:58.340
He's definitely the type that
ate his own boogers as a kid.

04:59.070 --> 05:00.420
And only a name here?

05:00.420 --> 05:02.880
I can't stand high-and-mighty dudes.

05:03.560 --> 05:06.840
I bet he likes setting 
oil-slicked gulls on fire.

05:08.820 --> 05:11.680
I always get stuck with 
unfortunate circumstances.

05:11.680 --> 05:14.440
She took one look and sighed.

05:14.440 --> 05:16.170
Are we going somewhere from here?

05:17.520 --> 05:20.130
We do have all three of you together.

05:20.130 --> 05:23.180
Not to mention, two of you 
are from the countryside.

05:23.360 --> 05:24.590
So of course we're going

05:24.590 --> 05:25.930
on a tour of Tokyo!

05:25.930 --> 05:31.440
Tokyo

05:26.150 --> 05:29.040
Tokyo! Tokyo! Tokyo!

05:29.040 --> 05:31.110
We love Tokyo!

05:31.110 --> 05:31.610
Huh?

05:31.610 --> 05:33.350
TDL! I want to go to TDL!

05:33.350 --> 05:35.570
Idiot! TDL's in Chiba!

05:35.570 --> 05:37.270
Let's go to Chinatown, Sensei!

05:37.270 --> 05:39.340
Chinatown's in Yokohama!

05:39.340 --> 05:41.340
Yokohama's part of Tokyo!

05:41.340 --> 05:43.040
Don't you know that? Look at a map!

05:43.040 --> 05:45.450
The hell?! Quit spouting nonsense!

05:43.040 --> 05:45.450
I will now announce our destination.

05:46.450 --> 05:51.960
Roppongi

05:46.620 --> 05:49.470
Roppongi!

05:49.470 --> 05:51.600
Roppongi?!

05:54.680 --> 05:56.120
There's a curse here.

05:56.830 --> 05:58.380
You liar!

05:58.380 --> 05:59.800
This isn't even Roppongi!

05:59.800 --> 06:01.600
You were toying with us country folk!

06:02.160 --> 06:04.780
There's a big cemetery nearby.

06:04.780 --> 06:08.090
The double whammy of that and an 
abandoned building brought out a curse.

06:08.110 --> 06:11.610
Who does he think is responsible 
for the rice he gets to eat, huh?!

06:08.360 --> 06:10.570
So they really do pop up 
more often around graves?

06:11.900 --> 06:13.640
The issue isn't the cemetery itself.

06:13.640 --> 06:18.040
It's the fact that people 
associate cemeteries with fear.

06:18.040 --> 06:20.630
Oh, it was the same 
for schools, too, wasn't it?

06:20.630 --> 06:23.610
Hold up. He didn't even know that yet?

06:24.210 --> 06:25.080
To be honest...

06:27.990 --> 06:30.630
He swallowed a special-grade cursed object?!

06:31.230 --> 06:32.910
Gross! Unbelievable!

06:32.910 --> 06:34.360
That's so unsanitary and disgusting!

06:34.360 --> 06:35.700
No way, no way, no way, no way!

06:35.700 --> 06:36.850
What?!

06:36.850 --> 06:37.880
I agree with her.

06:38.090 --> 06:40.560
I want to know what all of you are capable of.

06:40.560 --> 06:42.760
Just think of this as a field test.

06:43.240 --> 06:44.390
Nobara, Yuuji,

06:44.760 --> 06:47.300
you two go exorcise the 
curse inside that building.

06:47.300 --> 06:47.960
Geh.

06:48.710 --> 06:52.240
Huh? But I thought only curses 
could exorcise curses, right?

06:52.590 --> 06:54.640
I can't use any jujutsu yet.

06:54.970 --> 06:58.000
You're basically half a curse already.

06:58.000 --> 07:00.160
There's cursed energy 
flowing throughout your body.

07:00.160 --> 07:04.150
Though controlling that energy isn't 
something you can learn overnight,

07:04.150 --> 07:05.320
so use this.

07:07.750 --> 07:09.470
It's the cursed tool, Slaughter Demon.

07:09.470 --> 07:11.470
It's a weapon imbued with cursed energy.

07:11.470 --> 07:13.140
It'll work on curses, too.

07:14.560 --> 07:15.530
Lame.

07:18.430 --> 07:19.940
Oh, one more thing.

07:21.130 --> 07:22.860
Don't let Sukuna out.

07:24.230 --> 07:27.520
If you use him, you'll get rid 
of all the curses nearby in a flash,

07:27.920 --> 07:30.290
but you'll also drag everyone around into it.

07:30.290 --> 07:32.390
Got it. I won't let Sukuna out.

07:34.490 --> 07:35.870
Hurry it up.

07:35.870 --> 07:36.740
Yeah, yeah.

07:36.740 --> 07:38.100
Go on, now!

07:50.490 --> 07:52.100
I think I'll go, too.

07:52.100 --> 07:55.250
Don't push yourself. You're still recovering.

07:55.570 --> 07:57.780
But someone needs to keep 
an eye on Itadori, right?

07:58.190 --> 07:59.210
True.

07:59.690 --> 08:03.630
But the one we're testing 
this time is Nobara.

08:03.630 --> 08:05.190
What a pain.

08:05.430 --> 08:08.650
Why do I have to deal with curses 
after coming all the way to Tokyo?

08:08.650 --> 08:11.120
Huh? Didn't you come here to exorcise curses?

08:11.720 --> 08:14.660
Let's save some time and split up.

08:14.660 --> 08:18.600
I'll start from the top and go floor by floor. 
You start from the bottom.

08:18.860 --> 08:21.660
Let's get this over with quick 
and grab some sushi from Ginza.

08:21.660 --> 08:22.860
Hold on a minute.

08:22.860 --> 08:24.630
Let's take this a bit more seriously.

08:24.630 --> 08:26.410
Curses are dangerous, you know.

08:30.140 --> 08:32.950
I don't wanna hear it from someone 
who was a normie until recently!

08:32.950 --> 08:34.200
Now get moving!

08:36.330 --> 08:39.370
Your emotions have been 
all over the place today!

08:39.370 --> 08:41.130
This is why girls don't like you!

08:41.470 --> 08:43.700
How did you know they don't like me?!

08:44.170 --> 08:47.570
Are you even popular enough to talk? Bitch.

08:58.010 --> 09:03.570
Do... you need... a receipt?

09:03.810 --> 09:05.140
It's a curse!

09:26.730 --> 09:30.170
Yeah, I can really move!

09:31.770 --> 09:33.020
That Yuuji...

09:34.070 --> 09:35.390
He's missing a few up here.

09:35.870 --> 09:37.290
He has no hesitation

09:37.290 --> 09:42.050
when it comes to killing these things 
that take the form of living creatures,

09:42.050 --> 09:44.540
albeit bizarre-looking ones, to try to kill him.

09:46.700 --> 09:50.460
And it's not like he's been familiar 
with curses for a long time, like you.

09:50.650 --> 09:54.460
This is a boy who used to 
live a normal high school life.

09:55.310 --> 09:59.410
You've seen plenty of jujutsu sorcerers,
even those with talent,

09:59.410 --> 10:02.300
give up in frustration because
 they couldn't conquer

10:02.300 --> 10:04.300
their fear or disgust, haven't you?

10:06.420 --> 10:09.750
So today I want to confirm how crazy she is.

10:11.610 --> 10:13.770
Hey, you, curse.

10:19.750 --> 10:23.690
I mean you, mannequin in the center. 
You actually think you're hidden there?

10:26.960 --> 10:29.400
If you won't come out, 
I'll just exorcise you there.

10:30.010 --> 10:32.610
But Kugisaki has experience, right?

10:32.610 --> 10:34.250
Little late for that now, isn't it?

10:34.530 --> 10:37.370
Curses are born from human minds.

10:37.660 --> 10:41.150
So their strength and numbers grow 
in proportion to the population.

11:00.050 --> 11:02.150
Do you think Nobara understands...

11:04.410 --> 11:08.320
that curses in Tokyo are on a different 
level than those in the countryside?

11:19.990 --> 11:22.490
Kugisaki

11:27.100 --> 11:29.860
Curses are born from human minds.

11:27.990 --> 11:30.500
Broken Van

11:27.990 --> 11:30.500
Filth

11:27.990 --> 11:30.500
Serves you right

11:27.990 --> 11:30.500
Go back to Tokyo

11:27.990 --> 11:30.500
Leave

11:30.560 --> 11:34.000
So their strength and numbers grow 
in proportion to the population.

11:35.210 --> 11:39.560
Curses in Tokyo are on a different 
level than those in the countryside.

11:47.170 --> 11:49.520
You might want to pull those out...

11:54.940 --> 11:57.030
or my cursed energy will flow into you.

12:05.160 --> 12:06.560
Nailed it.

12:18.810 --> 12:20.300
A child?

12:20.770 --> 12:24.320
Must have snuck in for some fun 
and encountered the curse.

12:27.760 --> 12:31.750
Hey, it's all right now. Come on out.

12:33.650 --> 12:34.980
Huh?!

12:38.820 --> 12:43.130
I guess it's true that kids don't 
warm up to beautiful women.

12:43.130 --> 12:44.320
Guess I'll call Itadori.

12:44.320 --> 12:45.070
Wait!

12:46.880 --> 12:48.310
Don't leave me here!

13:07.660 --> 13:09.070
It's taking him hostage?

13:10.750 --> 13:13.290
This curse has intelligence?!

13:13.290 --> 13:17.520
When I say "level," I don't just mean 
the amount of cursed energy they have.

13:18.250 --> 13:19.690
It's their cunning.

13:19.690 --> 13:23.570
Monsters that have gained wisdom will 
often force cruel choices upon you...

13:24.930 --> 13:28.290
with the weight of human lives in the balance.

13:28.690 --> 13:30.260
Damn it, damn it, damn it!

13:30.260 --> 13:32.240
Damn it!

13:32.670 --> 13:35.490
This curse isn't even all that strong!

13:35.790 --> 13:37.000
Grade 4...

13:37.000 --> 13:39.450
Maybe even lower, like a low grade 3!

13:40.640 --> 13:42.800
But it's aware of that!

13:42.800 --> 13:45.970
That's why it chose to take a hostage!

13:47.890 --> 13:49.470
Calm yourself down.

13:50.480 --> 13:53.920
If I die, the child dies, too.

13:54.340 --> 13:57.510
But if the child dies, I won't die.

13:59.410 --> 14:06.400
Logically speaking, 
it's better if I survive, at least!

14:12.120 --> 14:13.300
I'm unarmed.

14:13.730 --> 14:15.490
Let the boy go.

14:21.880 --> 14:23.560
I'm such an idiot!

14:24.210 --> 14:26.750
See? It's not letting him go at all!

14:31.150 --> 14:34.720
I wish I could have seen 
Saori-chan one last time.

14:38.750 --> 14:40.870
Huh? I missed?

14:54.150 --> 14:55.310
You okay?

14:55.310 --> 14:56.200
Uh-huh.

14:59.860 --> 15:00.850
It's getting away!

15:00.850 --> 15:01.920
I don't think so!

15:01.920 --> 15:02.500
Itadori!

15:02.520 --> 15:03.780
Give me that arm!

15:03.780 --> 15:04.520
Huh?

15:07.690 --> 15:08.480
I'll exorcise it.

15:08.480 --> 15:09.330
Hold on.

15:11.290 --> 15:12.460
A straw doll?

15:12.460 --> 15:13.520
Creepy.

15:16.960 --> 15:18.380
Straw Doll Technique:

15:20.450 --> 15:21.580
Resonance!

15:30.760 --> 15:31.920
Nice.

15:31.920 --> 15:33.460
She's crazy, all right.

15:39.100 --> 15:40.060
We won.

15:47.000 --> 15:51.010
This bridge is dangerous
due to deterioration from age
and can no longer be used.

15:56.920 --> 15:59.010
When I was in first grade,

16:00.230 --> 16:02.990
Saori-chan moved to our village from Tokyo.

16:15.600 --> 16:18.530
She was as cute as a doll,

16:19.500 --> 16:22.550
and as kind as a nun.

16:24.000 --> 16:27.000
Sticker Book

16:30.910 --> 16:35.870
Yet Saori-chan was 
ostracized by the villagers.

16:39.760 --> 16:42.480
"She thinks country folk are dumb," they said,

16:42.760 --> 16:45.480
letting themselves get paranoid,

16:45.480 --> 16:47.480
We Protest the Kitagawa Highway Extension!

16:46.380 --> 16:47.480
and in the end...

16:51.510 --> 16:52.820
they drove her out.

16:51.510 --> 16:56.490
Home for Sale

16:56.490 --> 17:00.490
Broken Van

16:56.490 --> 17:00.490
Filth

16:56.490 --> 17:00.490
Serves you right

16:56.490 --> 17:00.490
Go back to Tokyo

16:56.490 --> 17:00.490
Leave

16:56.830 --> 16:59.200
Calling it sickening wouldn't be enough.

17:03.970 --> 17:06.760
She brought all these homemade 
sweets I'd never heard of and said,

17:07.130 --> 17:11.790
"The ones from the bakery are even better," 
with a smile as she treated me to them.

17:15.010 --> 17:18.260
This bridge is dangerous
due to deterioration from age
and can no longer be used.

17:16.140 --> 17:19.980
If I had stayed in that village...

17:22.300 --> 17:23.840
This is why I told you

17:23.840 --> 17:26.500
it's dangerous to go alone and 
you need to take it seriously!

17:26.500 --> 17:29.330
You never said it was dangerous to go alone!

17:29.330 --> 17:30.990
I... didn't?!

17:30.990 --> 17:34.950
And what have you been eating that lets you 
punch through a wall with your bare hand?!

17:35.190 --> 17:36.960
It wasn't reinforced concrete!

17:36.960 --> 17:39.900
Even if it was, that'd still be 
impossible for most people!

17:41.280 --> 17:42.790
Most people?

17:43.680 --> 17:47.220
You know, you've asked me 
plenty of questions already,

17:47.220 --> 17:49.440
but why did you come to Jujutsu Tech?

17:49.440 --> 17:50.720
Why?

17:51.820 --> 17:53.760
Because I hate the countryside,

17:53.760 --> 17:55.930
and I wanted to live in Tokyo!

17:59.380 --> 18:03.870
This was the only way I could move to the city 
without having to worry about money!

18:03.870 --> 18:06.220
You can risk your life over that?

18:09.590 --> 18:10.850
I can.

18:15.120 --> 18:17.280
After all, it means being true to myself.

18:21.130 --> 18:24.410
If I had stayed in that village, 
I'd be as good as dead.

18:34.160 --> 18:38.220
Saori-chan, I made it to Tokyo.

18:43.200 --> 18:44.390
If we ever meet here,

18:45.610 --> 18:48.980
take me to that bakery you mentioned.

18:53.940 --> 18:57.680
So as far as that goes, I'm grateful to you, too.

18:57.680 --> 18:59.010
There wouldn't have been

18:59.010 --> 19:02.900
a bright future if I had died or 
I had been the only one to survive.

19:03.870 --> 19:04.930
Thanks.

19:05.880 --> 19:10.040
Well, having a more serious reason 
doesn't make anyone better than the rest.

19:10.320 --> 19:12.770
Okay, I've given you my 
thanks, so that's all over!

19:12.770 --> 19:14.720
We're even now!

19:14.720 --> 19:16.150
What's wrong with her?

19:17.500 --> 19:20.280
I live over there! Thanks again!

19:23.450 --> 19:26.560
Did you know I get into a 
foul mood when I'm hungry?

19:26.560 --> 19:28.720
When are you not in a foul mood?

19:30.110 --> 19:32.400
Good Joseph!

19:32.930 --> 19:34.820
We made sure the kid got home.

19:36.630 --> 19:38.450
Now shall we go grab some food?

19:39.520 --> 19:40.690
Steak!

19:40.690 --> 19:41.990
Sushi!

19:43.310 --> 19:45.200
Leave it all to me!

19:45.200 --> 19:46.050
And you, Megumi?

19:49.700 --> 19:51.130
Okay, let's go.

19:54.690 --> 19:58.030
Oh, I forgot about my 
biggest haul of the day.

19:58.290 --> 20:00.550
Hey, you, go fetch my things.

19:59.340 --> 20:01.130
Harajuku

19:59.380 --> 20:01.130
Coin Locker

20:00.550 --> 20:02.550
Huh? Why should I do it?

20:02.550 --> 20:04.270
I thought we were even.

20:04.270 --> 20:07.350
We won thanks to my cursed energy. 
Got a problem with that?

20:07.350 --> 20:09.670
What about my raw strength?

20:09.670 --> 20:11.950
Your monstrous power 
from eating weird shit?

20:11.950 --> 20:13.580
It's not just that!

20:13.580 --> 20:14.790
Right, Fushiguro?

20:15.920 --> 20:18.060
Huh? What's the matter, Fushiguro?

20:18.060 --> 20:18.830
Nothing.

20:18.830 --> 20:20.680
He's pouting because he 
didn't get to join in.

20:21.790 --> 20:23.090
What a child.

20:30.330 --> 20:36.920
Log: July 2018

20:30.890 --> 20:33.830
Log: July 2018.

20:33.330 --> 20:36.920
West Tokyo City
Eishuu Juvenile Detention Center

20:33.830 --> 20:35.130
West Tokyo City,

20:35.130 --> 20:36.920
Eishuu Juvenile Detention Center.

20:39.630 --> 20:42.420
In the sky above the exercise yard

20:39.630 --> 20:42.420
In the sky above the exercise yard.

20:44.710 --> 20:45.650
Hey...

20:47.180 --> 20:48.420
What's that?

20:49.820 --> 20:50.530
What?

20:50.810 --> 20:59.940
Unnamed Apparition of Potential Special Grade

20:51.070 --> 20:54.500
Unnamed Apparition 
of Potential Special Grade.

20:54.140 --> 20:59.940
Its curse womb was witnessed by several non-jujutsu sorcerers.

20:55.080 --> 20:59.090
Its curse womb was witnessed 
by several non-jujutsu sorcerers.

21:00.420 --> 21:02.370
That up there! Looks like an egg.

21:02.370 --> 21:04.110
What are you talking about?

